                <pb facs="0428" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v33/pg394"/>

                <head>175. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On April 15, 1967, Francis Bator, President’s Deputy Special Assistant for
                    National Security Affairs, testified before the President’s Task Force on
                    Government Organization. During a presentation that focused on the larger issue
                    of managing interdepartmental foreign pol icy-making, <pb facs="0429" n="395"
                        xml:id="pg395"/> Bator also commented on the specific foreign policy role of
                    the White House staff. For text of his notes on that part of his presentation,
                    see <ref target="#d118">Document 118</ref>, Part III, Role of the White House
                    Staff.</p>
            </div>
